Search "latest trends in wedding rentals" and most results talk about tablescapes, color palettes, lounge furniture, champagne walls, and catering trends. Malaga Event Gear (MEG) is an audio visual rental company. We don't stock or speak to any of that, and a page that pretended otherwise would not be honest. What we can cover, from our own catalog and booking patterns, is what is actually changing on the AV side of a Malaga wedding: which package couples pick most, how lighting choices split, and where wireless microphones have become the default rather than the extra. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview.

## Brief Overview

---

The real trend on MEG's side of a wedding isn't a new fixture or a new color, it's a booking pattern. The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/), which includes a live technician on site throughout the event, is our most requested package for weddings up to 80 guests, at 650 euros ex VAT. Alongside that, wireless microphones for speeches are now a standard expectation rather than an add on, and couples choosing between the Wedding Pack's warm static lighting and the [Eco Pack's](/packages/eco/) color changing spotlights are making a real, deliberate choice, not defaulting to one or the other.

## Key Highlights

---

-   Most "wedding rental trend" content covers decor, tablescapes, and catering. MEG is AV only, so this page stays inside what we can honestly speak to.
-   The Wedding Pack, technician included, is our most popular wedding package, a real signal from our own catalog rather than an industry wide claim.
-   Wireless microphones for speeches are now a default expectation, not an upgrade, on the packages that include them.
-   Warm static lighting versus color changing spotlights is a real choice couples make between the Wedding Pack and the Eco Pack. Full comparison lives in our [lighting ideas for wedding rentals](/blog/lighting-ideas-for-wedding-rentals/) guide.
-   The Eco Pack's smaller, self run setup is the closest honest answer we have for couples asking about a smaller footprint rental, not a certified sustainability program.

## What Most "Wedding Rental Trend" Guides Cover, and Why We Can't Speak to It

Search results for this keyword are dominated by full service rental and event planning sites listing color of the year palettes, lounge furniture groupings, champagne and neon walls, linens, tablescapes, and catering trends. None of that is inaccurate reporting on what those companies rent, it's just not what MEG rents. We supply sound, microphones, lighting, and an on site technician. We don't touch furniture, decor, linens, catering, tents, or bars. A trend page that borrowed those topics from a decor blog to look comprehensive would be describing someone else's inventory, so this page stays inside AV: what packages couples are actually booking, how lighting choices split, and what's become standard rather than optional in our own catalog.

## The Trend We Actually See: More Weddings Booking the Technician Included Package

The clearest pattern we can point to from our own catalog is the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) itself. It's marked as our most popular package, and it's one of only two packages we offer that includes a live technician on site for the whole event rather than a delivery, test, and self run setup. That technician handles sound levels through the ceremony, the microphone hand offs between reception speakers, and lighting through the night, work that used to be treated as an optional upgrade on smaller events but is now the default expectation on the package couples book most. Our [making the most of your wedding rentals](/blog/making-the-most-of-wedding-rentals/) guide covers how to brief that technician on your run of show once you've booked, so we won't repeat that depth here.

<InlineCTA />

## Static Warm Light or Color Changing Accents: A Real Choice, Not a Default

The other pattern worth naming honestly is how couples choose between our two lighting options. The Wedding Pack's fairy lights and warm LED strings give a fixed, warm glow for up to 80 guests, with the technician placing and monitoring them all night. The Eco Pack's RGBW color changing spotlights suit a smaller event, up to 50 guests, delivered and tested by our crew, then run without a technician for the rest of the event. Neither is an upgrade path from the other, they're two different looks for two different guest counts, and increasingly couples ask about both before deciding rather than assuming the bigger package automatically includes color changing light. It doesn't. Our [lighting ideas for wedding rentals](/blog/lighting-ideas-for-wedding-rentals/) guide has the full placement by placement breakdown, this page only needs to name that the choice itself is the trend.

## Wireless Microphones for Speeches, and What "Eco" Actually Means in Our Eco Pack

Professional wireless microphones for speeches and announcements are part of the Wedding Pack, and they've become an expected inclusion rather than a special request, since most receptions now run through several speakers, best man, maid of honor, parents, sometimes the couple, back to back rather than a single toast. That's a real shift from a rental company's perspective: a wired handheld mic passed hand to hand between speakers is no longer what most couples ask for.

On the sustainability side, we get asked about smaller footprint or eco friendly options often enough that it's worth being precise about what the Eco Pack actually is. It's a smaller setup, two speakers, one wired microphone, two light bars, self run once our crew delivers and tests it, sized for events up to 50 guests. That's a genuinely smaller installation than the Wedding Pack, but it isn't a certified sustainability program or a carbon offset claim, and we won't market it as one. If a smaller, simpler footprint is what you're after for a smaller guest count, the Eco Pack is the honest answer.

## What's Included

The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) costs 650 euros, ex VAT, for up to 80 guests, and includes:

-   A high end active PA sound system.
-   Fairy lights and warm LED strings for ambient lighting.
-   Professional wireless microphones for speeches and announcements.
-   Transport in Malaga and surrounding areas.
-   Professional setup and cabling.
-   A live technician on site throughout the event.
-   Post event teardown and pickup.

The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) costs 290 euros, ex VAT, for up to 50 guests, and includes 2 high quality active speakers, 1 wired dynamic microphone, 2 light bars with RGBW LED spotlights, and aesthetic cabling and professional setup, self run after our crew delivers and tests it. We equip both packages with premium professional brands, including Shure, QSC, and Martin. See exact, live pricing and the full breakdown, including both packages, on our [all in one wedding rental packages](/blog/all-in-one-wedding-rental-packages/) guide or our [packages page](/packages/).

